$BODY = <<<'HTML'
<h2>Why disclosure is the whole game</h2>
<p>Quantum in maintenance is a function of two variables: the needs of the claimant and the means of the payer. The first is easy to prove; the second is routinely concealed — salaries routed to family accounts, businesses run in a brother&rsquo;s name, rental income left off affidavits. The disclosure machinery exists because cross-examination alone cannot reconstruct a balance sheet. Documents can.</p>

<h2>The three layers of the machinery</h2>
<div class="flow">
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Layer one: the sworn affidavit.</strong> Both sides file a structured affidavit of assets, income and expenditure covering salary, business income, immovable property, vehicles, bank accounts, investments, liabilities and monthly outgoings — including dependants supported and litigation expenses. The affidavit is the baseline document against which every later disclosure is tested.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Layer two: directed production.</strong> Where the affidavit looks thin, the court can direct the party to produce the underlying records — income tax returns for recent assessment years, Form 16, salary slips, GST returns, and statements of every disclosed account. The request should be specific: named accounts, named years, named employers.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Layer three: third-party summons.</strong> The decisive layer. Under the general powers to summon documents and witnesses — Section 94 BNSS on the criminal side, Order XVI CPC before the Family Courts, supplemented by the Family Courts Act&rsquo;s liberal evidence regime — the court can call for records straight from the employer, the bank, or the income tax department. Records obtained from the source cannot be curated by the party.</div>
</div>

<h2>Meeting the usual objections</h2>
<p><strong>&ldquo;The ITR is confidential.&rdquo;</strong> Confidentiality yields to relevance. The respondent&rsquo;s income is not collateral material in a maintenance case; it is the fact in issue. Courts have consistently permitted summoning of tax records in matrimonial litigation, and the Family Courts Act expressly loosens formal evidence rules so that such material can be received and acted upon.</p>
<p><strong>&ldquo;The business is not mine.&rdquo;</strong> Where income is routed through relatives, lifestyle evidence fills the gap: the car driven, the school fees paid, the residence maintained, foreign travel, credit card statements. A court assessing means is entitled to prefer the standard of living actually enjoyed over the poverty pleaded on affidavit.</p>
<p><strong>&ldquo;I am unemployed.&rdquo;</strong> An able-bodied respondent is presumed capable of earning at least at the level of his qualifications and work history. Courts in Delhi routinely peg such respondents to minimum wage or to their last drawn salary rather than accepting zero.</p>

<h2>The cost of concealment</h2>
<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><strong>Adverse inference.</strong> Suppression of accounts or non-filing lets the court accept the claimant&rsquo;s estimate and fix quantum against the concealing party.</div>
  <div class="tile"><strong>Quantum consequences.</strong> Concealed savings and undisclosed credits, once exposed through summoned statements, routinely move interim maintenance upward — and can justify enhancement later.</div>
  <div class="tile"><strong>Perjury exposure.</strong> A false affidavit is sworn testimony. The court may initiate perjury proceedings, a risk that disciplines disclosure far more effectively than argument.</div>
  <div class="tile"><strong>Defence struck off.</strong> Persistent default in paying interim maintenance can cost the defaulter the right to contest, leaving quantum to be decided on the claimant&rsquo;s material.</div>
</div>

<h2>A working checklist for the claimant&rsquo;s side</h2>
<div class="check">
  <p>Seek directions for affidavits of assets and income at the first effective hearing — not after pleadings close.</p>
  <p>Serve a specific production list: ITRs with computation sheets for three years, Form 16/16A, GST returns, statements of all accounts named in the affidavit.</p>
  <p>Apply for third-party summons to the employer and bankers where production is evasive; ask for records from the source, not copies from the party.</p>
  <p>Assemble lifestyle evidence in parallel — vehicles, school fees, travel, rent actually paid — to test the affidavit&rsquo;s credibility.</p>
  <p>Where the affidavit is demonstrably false, seek consequences in terms: adverse inference on quantum and, in egregious cases, perjury action.</p>
</div>
<div class="note">The machinery works both ways. A respondent facing an inflated claim is equally entitled to summon the claimant&rsquo;s employment records and bank statements, since maintenance also reflects the claimant&rsquo;s own income and earning capacity. Honest, early, documented disclosure is the cheapest strategy either side can adopt.</div>
